name: Gluon
version: "__VERSION__"
tagline: Your home server, at a glance
description: >-
  Gluon is a home for this server. A start page you can arrange with live widgets,
  a plain-words status of everything running, and alerts that reach your phone.


  It manages the parts CasaOS and Umbrel leave out: disks and mount points
  (with drive health), public addresses through Caddy, a file manager with
  pinned folders and a trash, live network and process diagnostics, and
  accounts for the household with only the apps and folders you share.


  Gluon drives the host directly, so it runs privileged on the host network.
  Open it on port 8130; the first visit asks for a one-time setup code, which is
  in the app's logs.
